\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Mean gains of PACE vs. mean-local comparator restricted to cohorts meeting the necessary data requirements across budgets (58 / 47 / 15 targets at $N \leq $ 750 / 2000 / 20k). Lines and 95\% CIs denote average change vs. comparator and bootstrapped CIs within the fixed cohort of targets (only targets satisfying data-requirements shown). Shading/borders on lines for clarity only - comparisons should be made along-budget within a given cohort, noting differences across cohorts (also) depend on cohort definition and contained targets/CIs depend on this fixed cohort. Note that in the last plot, the TON\_IoT effect is fixed under corpus-stratified sampling given it contains 1 target.}}{24}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:budgets}{{4}{24}{Mean gains of PACE vs. mean-local comparator restricted to cohorts meeting the necessary data requirements across budgets (58 / 47 / 15 targets at $N \leq $ 750 / 2000 / 20k). Lines and 95\% CIs denote average change vs. comparator and bootstrapped CIs within the fixed cohort of targets (only targets satisfying data-requirements shown). Shading/borders on lines for clarity only - comparisons should be made along-budget within a given cohort, noting differences across cohorts (also) depend on cohort definition and contained targets/CIs depend on this fixed cohort. Note that in the last plot, the TON\_IoT effect is fixed under corpus-stratified sampling given it contains 1 target}{figure.4}{}}
